    affiliation: "Korea Institute of Science and Technology"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of KAN-DI, the acquisition at the core of the
  KAN-DoE framework. Bayesian optimization uses a pruned Kolmogorov–Arnold
  network as the Gaussian-process prior mean and a composite acquisition
  function (exploitation, discrimination, uniformity), so that one
  optimization loop maximizes the response and identifies its governing
  descriptors at the same time. Descriptor importance is the average
  gradient energy (AGE), the squared partial derivative of the closed-form
  KAN response averaged over the candidate pool.
